meta {
  name: 12 Assign OS To Device
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/os-assignments
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "os_version_id": {{osVersionId}},
    "device_id": {{demoDeviceId}},
    "immediate": true
  }
}

vars:post-response {
  osAssignmentId: res.body.id
}

docs {
  `POST /os-assignments` — the money shot: assign the new OS version to the
  scanner IPC. `immediate: true` tells the orchestrator to apply it right
  away instead of waiting for a maintenance window — on a real slicing line
  you would leave it out and let the update land in the next window.

  **Watch the log stream tab:** the IPC downloads and stages the image in the
  background, then reboots into it — the gap in the heartbeat logs is the
  near-zero downtime, and the cheese keeps moving.

  Note: the device applies its *first* active assignment. If it already has
  an older one, delete it first (*User API → OS Assignments*).
}
